---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../i18n';
import { resolvePageSeo } from '../config/seo';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ContactSupportSection from '../components/ContactSupportSection.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const seo = resolvePageSeo('/support/');
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Support', path: '/support/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  logoAlt="Support – site logo"
  jsonLd={[
    webPageSchema({
      name: t.support.title,
      description: t.support.subtitle,
      url: '/support/',
    }),
    breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs),
  ]}
>
  <section class="border-b border-border bg-muted/20 py-8 md:py-10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactSupportSection titleId="support-page-title" showTicketTips />

  <article class="content-markdown support-page-shell border-t border-border bg-muted/10 py-10 md:py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
      <h2>Before you contact support</h2>
      <p>
        Start on the homepage hero for live plan previews (<strong>$35 monthly</strong> and <strong>$150 lifetime</strong> on the core bundle).
        Skim the <a href="/faq/">pre-purchase question list</a>, then walk through the
        <a href="/guides/system-requirements/">hardware requirements walkthrough</a> so tickets include hardware context instead of guesses.
      </p>
      <p>
        Checkout happens on the vendor site linked from the <a href="/go/">product checkout bridge</a>. arc-cheats.net publishes screenshots and affiliate bridges; license keys arrive from the vendor inbox named on your receipt.
      </p>
      <h2>Orders, licenses, and resends</h2>
      <p>
        Paste the full receipt, the email you used at checkout, and the product SKU exactly as printed. If a key never arrived, check spam and promotions folders before you request a resend.
      </p>
      <p>
        HWID reset requests need the old and new machine IDs when the vendor policy allows transfers. Optional utilities such as spoofers or DMA add-ons follow different refund rules—quote the line item from your cart.
      </p>
      <h2>Information to include in every ticket</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Windows version and build (Settings → System → About)</li>
        <li>GPU model and driver version</li>
        <li>Whether overlays are enabled and which module (ESP, aim, DMA)</li>
        <li>Screenshots of errors or misaligned HUD stills, capped at five files</li>
        <li>Timestamp and map name when crashes happen in-game</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Setup and performance troubleshooting</h2>
      <p>
        Compare your symptom with indoor and outdoor stills on the <a href="/arc-raiders-esp/">player and loot marker guide</a>.
        Flickering boxes often trace to frame dips; menu stutter may mean you need to lower graphics before enabling container filters.
      </p>
      <p>
        For aim module tuning, read <a href="/arc-raiders-aimbot/">FOV and smoothing field notes</a> so support does not re-explain defaults you can change client-side.
      </p>
      <p>
        Shoppers evaluating DMA should finish the <a href="/guides/cloud-dma-setup/">Cloud DMA preparation article</a> and attach BIOS or hypervisor notes when indoor radar drifts.
      </p>
      <h2>Ban and enforcement questions</h2>
      <p>
        We do not operate anti-cheat systems. For factual differences between account strikes and hardware flags, read the
        <a href="/arc-raiders-account-vs-hardware-ban/">account versus hardware enforcement guide</a> before you ask for reinstatement timelines.
      </p>
      <h2>Response expectations</h2>
      <p>
        Email replies are manual, often within one business day for US afternoons. Weekends and vendor patch days can add delay.
        Refund eligibility, chargebacks, and subscription cancellations follow the vendor policy linked at checkout—not this domain.
      </p>
      <h2>Affiliate and editorial questions</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about commissions or how we test screenshots belong on the
        <a href="/contact/">pre-checkout support walkthrough</a> or the <a href="/about/">independent product guides about page</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
      <p>
        Use the contact cards above for the billing inbox listed on your receipt. Include “ARC Raiders” in the subject so routing skips unrelated queues.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are filing a chargeback at the same time as a support ticket, note that vendors often pause license access until the dispute closes. Finish reading the vendor refund paragraph on your receipt before you escalate on two channels at once.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
